From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 117/119] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Clear no PM1 or GPE0 status from
 the SMI handler

With SCI_EN set, PM1 and GPE0 events raise an SCI, never an SMI#, and
the handler ignores their bits of SMI_STS. It cleared PM1_STS and
GPE0_STS all the same when those were the only bits set, "or the SMI#
would come again": it would not, as they did not raise it. An SMI# that
shows nothing else came from elsewhere (an IPI, a timeout), and the
clear threw away an event the OS had yet to see, the power button
pending as an SCI for one. Do as the common SMM code of soc/intel: mask
the two bits and leave the status registers to the OS.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c | 14 +++-----------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
index d77268801a..fb9ba87be3 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/smihandler.c
@@ -586,18 +586,10 @@ void southbridge_smi_handler(void)
 	 * power off. On S3 resume PM1_STS holds PWRBTN_STS when the power
 	 * button, or the EC through it, woke the system, and ramstage sends
 	 * APMC commands before the OS resumes (finalize, the vboot slot lock).
-	 * Should those events alone have raised this SMI#, clear them, or it
-	 * would come again.
+	 * They cannot have raised this SMI#, so nothing is left pending here.
 	 */
-	if (inl(get_pmbase() + PM1_CNT) & SCI_EN) {
-		const u32 os_events = smi_sts & (1 << PM1_STS_BIT | 1 << GPE0_STS_BIT);
-
-		smi_sts &= ~os_events;
-		if (os_events && !smi_sts) {
-			clear_pm1_status();
-			clear_gpe_status();
-		}
-	}
+	if (inl(get_pmbase() + PM1_CNT) & SCI_EN)
+		smi_sts &= ~(1 << PM1_STS_BIT | 1 << GPE0_STS_BIT);
 
 	/* Call SMI sub handler for each of the status bits */
 	for (i = 0; i < 31; i++) {
